  {
    "id": "944f20be9dc34b06",
    "text": "Air 4th-axis relief",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/Air/Manual/Air-4th-axis-relief"
  },
  {
    "id": "e1ec11a93e60fcbf",
    "text": "This case shows you how to use Carvera Air’s rotary axis to machine a 3D object. We don’t use dust collection for rotary axis machining, so we split the roughing and finishing process into two jobs. You should clean the dust between the two steps.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/Air/Manual/Air-4th-axis-relief"
  },
  {
    "id": "02e2a8cb8e2ac510",
    "text": "The Nefertiti sample model in this guide was from Thomas Roussel - Thingiverse: @lecaramel.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/Air/Manual/Air-4th-axis-relief"
  },
  {
    "id": "923e395fde35bcc9",
    "text": "Note: Please read the instruction manual carefully to understand how to install and use the 4th axis.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/Air/Manual/Air-4th-axis-relief"
  },
  {
    "id": "3d8585775d0e1293",
    "text": "Note：Some of the parameters for 4-axis and 3-axis machining are different: The 3-axis can be positioned using anchor point 1 or anchor point 2. The Y-axis position of the 4-axis is fixed, and the X-axis is positioned releative to the right edge of the headstock.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/Air/Manual/Air-4th-axis-relief"
  },
  {
    "id": "61549252378998b7",
    "text": "Note：We don’t use auto-leveling for 4-axis machining, and the auto z probe position is fixed.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/Air/Manual/Air-4th-axis-relief"
  },
  {
    "id": "d88fb05ee9be6db2",
    "text": "Note：We don’t use dust collection for 4-axis machining. Please remove the dust shoe.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/Air/Manual/Air-4th-axis-relief"
  },
  {
    "id": "bc120df08c94cd34",
